@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Overview
@chapter Overview

Hellmacs is designed for developers who write enterprise software on the
JVM (Spring Boot, Maven, Gradle, multi-module enterprise codebases) and want
a rock-solid, ultra-fast environment that respects GNU Emacs traditions.

Key objectives:
@enumerate
@item
@strong{Daily JVM Parity}: Deep code completion, refactoring, navigation,
diagnostics, test runners, debugging, and Spring Boot integration.
@item
@strong{Strict Startup Budget}: Starts in under 0.12 seconds with 60+ packages
byte-compiled ahead of time.
@item
@strong{Enterprise Ready}: Full support for corporate proxies, custom CA
truststores, internal artifact mirrors (Artifactory, Nexus), and 100% offline bundles.
@item
@strong{Zero Modal Hijacking}: Stock Emacs keybindings are preserved
completely. No modal editing, no Evil mode, no @kbd{SPC} leader hijacks.
@end enumerate

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node The 40-Year Purist Guarantee
@chapter The 40-Year Purist Guarantee

Every stock GNU Emacs keychord works exactly as documented in the official
GNU Emacs manual:
@itemize @bullet
@item @kbd{C-x C-f} finds files, @kbd{C-x b} switches buffers, @kbd{C-s} searches.
@item @kbd{M-x} executes commands, @kbd{C-g} cancels, @kbd{C-h} provides help.
@item @kbd{TAB} indents, @kbd{C-M-i} invokes completion-at-point.
@item @kbd{C-x 2}, @kbd{C-x 3}, @kbd{C-x 0}, @kbd{C-x 1}, @kbd{C-x o} manage windows.
@item @kbd{C-x t} manages tabs and workspaces.
@end itemize

Custom Hellmacs commands are grouped strictly under @kbd{C-c}, the prefix
reserved by GNU Emacs conventions for users:
@table @kbd
@item C-c h
Hellmacs core commands (@kbd{C-c h s} Altar, @kbd{C-c h f} Forge, @kbd{C-c h k} IntelliJ Finder, @kbd{C-c h i} Info manual).
@item C-c c
Code and compilation commands (@kbd{C-c c c} compile, @kbd{C-c c a} code actions, @kbd{C-c c r} rename).
@item C-c l
The Localleader: mode-specific commands (Java imports, refactorings, test runners).
@item C-c w
Workspace and tab management (@kbd{C-c w p} open project tab, @kbd{C-c w w} switch tab).
@item C-c t
Toggles (@kbd{C-c t w} tab-bar, @kbd{C-c t l} line numbers, @kbd{C-c t f} flymake).
@end table

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Installation and Profiles
@chapter Installation and Profiles

Hellmacs is installed via the @command{bin/hellmacs-install} script:
@example
git clone https://github.com/petrolal/hellmacs.git ~/.config/emacs
bin/hellmacs install
@end example

@section Profiles
Hellmacs supports isolated profiles:
@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{default}: The primary configuration located at @file{~/.config/hellmacs/}.
@item @strong{dev}: Isolated development testing profile in @file{profiles/dev/}.
@item @strong{safe-mode}: Clean baseline profile with only built-in packages.
@end itemize

Run commands on specific profiles using @code{-p NAME}:
@example
bin/hellmacs -p dev sync
bin/hellmacs -p dev doctor
@end example

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Daily JVM Workflow
@chapter Daily JVM Workflow

Hellmacs provides deep language support for the complete JVM ecosystem.

@section Java (@code{:lang java})
Powered by Eclipse JDTLS, java-debug, and Spring Boot Tools:
@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Code Completion}: Semantic member completion, type hints, Lombok annotations.
@item @strong{Refactoring}: Extract method (@kbd{C-c l m}), extract variable (@kbd{C-c l v}), extract constant (@kbd{C-c l c}), generate getters/setters (@kbd{C-c l g}).
@item @strong{Spring Boot}: Bean navigation, application properties completion, `@code{@@Autowired}` cross-references.
@item @strong{Testing}: Run JUnit test at point (@kbd{C-c l t t}) or test class (@kbd{C-c l t T}).
@end itemize

@section Kotlin, Clojure, Groovy, and Scala
@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Kotlin} (@code{:lang kotlin}): Kotlin Language Server with Gradle/Maven support.
@item @strong{Clojure} (@code{:lang clojure}): CIDER REPL integration with @code{clojure-lsp}.
@item @strong{Groovy} (@code{:lang groovy}): Groovy Language Server built from pinned Gradle verification.
@item @strong{Scala} (@code{:lang scala}): Metals language server and sbt build tool integration.
@end itemize

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node IntelliJ Parity & Key Finder
@chapter IntelliJ Parity & Key Finder

For developers migrating from JetBrains IntelliJ IDEA, Hellmacs includes the
interactive IntelliJ Key Finder:
@example
M-x hellmacs-where-is-intellij
@end example
Shortcut: @kbd{C-c h k} or @kbd{C-c h ?}.

Type any IntelliJ shortcut (e.g. @kbd{Shift-F6}, @kbd{Ctrl-Alt-L}, @kbd{Double Shift}, @kbd{Ctrl-N})
to immediately see the equivalent GNU Emacs keychord and execute the command.

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Enhanced Dired & Projectile
@chapter Enhanced Dired & Projectile

@section Enhanced Dired (@code{:emacs dired})
File management in Hellmacs is enhanced with:
@itemize @bullet
@item Colored filetype glyphs via @code{nerd-icons-dired}.
@item Batch file renaming as editable text: press @kbd{r} or @kbd{C-x C-q} in Dired to enter @code{wdired-mode}.
@item Quick sorting menu: press @kbd{S} in Dired to sort by name, size, date, or extension.
@item Automatic reuse of Dired buffers to keep buffer lists clean.
@end itemize

@section Projectile (@code{:tools projectile})
Fast project exploration and buffer management:
@itemize @bullet
@item @kbd{C-c p f}: Find file in project with fuzzy search.
@item @kbd{C-c p s r}: Ripgrep search across project.
@item @kbd{C-c p b}: Switch between project-specific buffers.
@end itemize

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Workspaces
@chapter Workspaces

The @code{:ui workspaces} module provides clean project workspace isolation
using Emacs' native @code{tab-bar-mode}:
@table @kbd
@item C-x t 2
Open a new workspace tab.
@item C-x t 0
Close current workspace tab.
@item C-x t o
Cycle to next workspace tab.
@item C-x t p
Open or switch to a project in its own dedicated workspace tab.
@item C-x t r
Rename workspace tab.
@item C-x t b
Switch workspace tab by fuzzy search.
@item C-c t w
Toggle workspace tab bar visibility.
@end table

Each tab automatically formats with project indicators and nerd-icons glyphs.

