@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Enterprise & Team Layer
@chapter Enterprise & Team Layer

Hellmacs is built for corporate network requirements.

@section Team Layer
Share configuration across your engineering team with @code{$HELLMACS_TEAM_DIR}:
@example
export HELLMACS_TEAM_DIR="/path/to/shared/company-hellmacs-layer"
@end example
Or install directly from git:
@example
bin/hellmacs install --team https://git.internal.corp/team-hellmacs.git
@end example

@section Proxies and Custom CAs
In @file{init.el}:
@example
(setq hellmacs-net-proxy "http://proxy.corp.internal:8080"
      hellmacs-net-ca-file "/etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/corp-root.crt")
@end example

@section Offline Bundles
Install on air-gapped systems with zero internet access:
@example
bin/hellmacs install --from-bundle /path/to/hellmacs-bundle.tar.gz
@end example

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node CLI Reference
@chapter CLI Reference

The @command{bin/hellmacs} CLI provides complete environment management:
@table @command
@item sync
Download, build, and byte-compile all active packages and language servers.
@item upgrade
Pull latest Hellmacs git commits/tags, update packages, and re-sync.
@item config
Inspect and add newly introduced default modules (@command{config --add-defaults}).
@item doctor
Comprehensive health verification of Emacs, SDKs, JDKs, servers, and tools.
@item profile
List and sync multi-profile environments (@command{profile list}, @command{profile sync --all}).
@item plugins
Manage community and third-party modules (@command{plugins list}, @command{plugins enable}).
@item bundle
Create self-contained offline deployment packages.
@item doctor --network
Validate connectivity through configured proxies, mirrors, and corporate CAs.
@end table

@c -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node Diagnostics and Doctor
@chapter Diagnostics and Doctor

Run @command{bin/hellmacs doctor} at any time to verify system health:
@example
bin/hellmacs doctor
@end example

Doctor checks:
@itemize @bullet
@item GNU Emacs version (30.1+, 31.1+) and native compilation support.
@item Installed JDKs (via SDKMAN!, system PATH, or asdf) and JDTLS compatibility.
@item Build systems (Gradle wrappers, Maven daemon, Maven wrappers).
@item Language server binaries (Eclipse JDTLS, Kotlin LS, Clojure LSP, Groovy LS, LemMinX, Docker LS, Marksman, etc.).
@item Tree-sitter ABI grammars and font icon availability.
@end itemize

